WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.990
Turn on a tap, and water
flows for almost nothing.

2
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.450
Now picture a tiny diamond.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.820
Its price can be enormous.

4
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.530
Here is the strange part.

5
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.550
Water is vital to life,

6
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.340
and diamonds are not.

7
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.640
Economists call this the paradox of value.

8
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.150
So why does the thing that
keeps us alive cost so little,

9
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.120
while a sparkly stone costs so much?

10
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.620
In this mission, you'll
measure satisfaction in utils,

11
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.870
one slice of pizza at a time.

12
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:34.420
Then you'll use that idea to explain
why demand curves slope downward,

13
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:38.220
and test how far the model of
rational choice can be trusted.

14
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: find out why diamonds
cost so much more than water.
